{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_15a63447d967a606bc5c76e6ef7b41bea5d357a74ec95e612d05a22addcd95d7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"2389-research/simmer@73089c6f2224 snapshot 0c3030b83e9b2b41","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_371ac24e584cee82a5bf74669d5fe09468ab81ed86e3ff06da1035a9b0ff9b3b","slc_4a8fdc7e8852f44f932dd00b925d33ada7ef389a876521444212bcc8d2ee6742","slc_66b3a1e67ec31922ed980c873e16ec213edf41528069abb8fb8856e1956e0f5a","slc_e21a842c5e54c0099efca4f040449c8631b5befdac3877e559e6a172fdbefbee"],"source_ids":["src_0a68d8eb30225280b1845adee6cad635","src_f5aca28d20435bad9211aa6f4356a910"],"text":"In workspace mode, each iteration is snapshotted as a git commit, enabling diffing and rollback via git checkout to the best iteration's commit; single-file mode instead writes iteration-N-candidate.md files.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_19d16fc3eed3a74fe5aa8ab417765ed6b55fdbddf11ea0c9477f2e3804b6d461","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"2389-research/simmer@73089c6f2224 snapshot 0c3030b83e9b2b41","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4a3f9d59f11038d6f48975805c9d1c7607fc417bd266405769ab8f9a80e08a69","slc_6754725e72145f1a7a362b415f24a9aa27221a406fcc84c2a4d0ab575b105bdd","slc_c53038ba4fce10468bc2de579bfda517f8013121227c96121336c5867c48930b"],"source_ids":["src_f5aca28d20435bad9211aa6f4356a910"],"text":"Simmer auto-selects between a single judge and a multi-judge board based on complexity (e.g., ≤2 criteria vs. code or pipelines), and offers upgrading to the board mid-run if a single-judge run plateaus for 3 iterations.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_22913fc9380dc88e10656c0d72b8e2f98434dbe710ad9124bb58f5684c907b20","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"2389-research/simmer@73089c6f2224 snapshot 0c3030b83e9b2b41","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_35d5143be3ca4b62cc11787be4dab7eb53d8e0e064c5f2a98eec8b0111b547ec"],"source_ids":["src_f5aca28d20435bad9211aa6f4356a910"],"text":"The reflect subskill tracks the best candidate seen so far; if an iteration regresses, the best-so-far is preserved and the final result.md contains the highest-scoring candidate rather than the latest one.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_23e6a84256505495090b9aeae1b03c516f193e0bc1653cf4d3a688778e79214f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"2389-research/simmer@73089c6f2224 snapshot 0c3030b83e9b2b41","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3f0203321d373e28716901e9e81eff4acaffdaf3bae946f7b506077bf61b76f6"],"source_ids":["src_f5aca28d20435bad9211aa6f4356a910"],"text":"Installation is via Claude Code plugin marketplace commands: adding the 2389-research/claude-plugins marketplace and installing simmer@2389-research.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_29e63738ba42a86cb835c97cc85c5529d371a68cb4e91697ee630f49eac035dc","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"2389-research/simmer@73089c6f2224 snapshot 0c3030b83e9b2b41","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1323a5611062ffbdb9f864f5357c5746d5eaed62f5ae94bebb1633f8dd469c26","slc_916e07971282d9c219ba6ffaebbbe09194ce78b42dc495780fee52ef17c4f4f5","slc_c01978335eaf73f9b475216f664cb707f3c987091a0bb81b079eb3b380fff4f7"],"source_ids":["src_0a68d8eb30225280b1845adee6cad635","src_f5aca28d20435bad9211aa6f4356a910"],"text":"Each iteration targets one direction via ASI (Actionable Side Information), the single highest-leverage fix; for workspace targets this becomes one coherent multi-file direction rather than unrelated changes.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_75deef1acefc2a0832c6825d24a251d9f426b3839bf279e076183a8a6ed810ed","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"2389-research/simmer@73089c6f2224 snapshot 0c3030b83e9b2b41","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_fbf40aef347ef410e07326e20aea77a0eb98c845dc364339cbc606b54490909f"],"source_ids":["src_f5aca28d20435bad9211aa6f4356a910"],"text":"Default iteration count is 3 rounds per batch, after which the tool asks whether to continue; users can request a specific count or stop early at any prompt.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ac0e3569366ae30daaae55e550182ccc2f80b45025667969eca53471c260cc92","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"2389-research/simmer@73089c6f2224 snapshot 0c3030b83e9b2b41","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_49a97af2691e2c7733f74b93691089d4912f485e33fb1a546bab9c0314e42348","slc_595a66457aab89de1015958eea7156dc207793661b3ef6672616f6236da84fda","slc_5ec81b2b3f31f657316e02b6b81bdb45927b297455c28489ce62f3649f07d7bb","slc_f1f42b966db9cdb7d29eb061725df845cefa28bb22380489be5cde94ed86f3d3"],"source_ids":["src_0a68d8eb30225280b1845adee6cad635","src_f5aca28d20435bad9211aa6f4356a910"],"text":"Three evaluation modes are supported: judge-only (default, for text artifacts), runnable (judge interprets a script's output), and hybrid (both). There is no format contract on evaluator output; the judge reads whatever the script produces.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_db87ddd91a25d7a744e6ba4bdb4aec304e6c0e477b75a2a1ff3d8cd328652708","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"2389-research/simmer@73089c6f2224 snapshot 0c3030b83e9b2b41","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9ee7e66b61bb12eab29a55bfa9bf4b75e01f4bec63692cc4ff6b3fad17db44f7"],"source_ids":["src_f5aca28d20435bad9211aa6f4356a910"],"text":"Context isolation is a stated design principle: the generator does not see scores and the judge does not see previous scores, so each role gets only the context it needs to avoid bias.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e6afb2e8f6c0156b8d559c053f67c7e85152f398eb4d20a36c1ca85fddb43b4d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=relevance","setting":"2389-research/simmer@73089c6f2224 snapshot 0c3030b83e9b2b41","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_11dd015699391c9cc132d6232ec32a026db227842e5163f2090ea613f098b32a","slc_492ad2d8d73c0aa93fd1ade2ed9346288c67090d1ee674ac100eb750fd5aa77d","slc_8ba1f2fd512506c4ae03882a2877caae84e698cba565fea5a0531ff6aff3cb4d"],"source_ids":["src_f5aca28d20435bad9211aa6f4356a910"],"text":"Simmer belongs to the test-kitchen skill family but is independently installable, alongside cookoff (parallel implementation competition) and omakase-off (parallel design exploration); simmer is the serial-iteration counterpart.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f293ce370837c3c5494befae45ffd49835a60461c28f0d1c9134fff2e0662213","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"2389-research/simmer@73089c6f2224 snapshot 0c3030b83e9b2b41","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_35a0d64398e308429891acaa0e360b817519d270ce4b75ce9596d2152fa368ef"],"source_ids":["src_0a68d8eb30225280b1845adee6cad635"],"text":"The v2 design spec extends the refinement loop with pluggable evaluation, multi-file workspace targets, expanded ASI, and background constraints; all additions are opt-in and default behavior matches v1.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f75c028f5f61cf41f6187459b394feb7c3bf5006377793af43235cbb3a9aabfb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"2389-research/simmer@73089c6f2224 snapshot 0c3030b83e9b2b41","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b06cbdb905f78cf178d5ea2265fc699e614d554ab47cb8bb78759bd1a591c1ff","slc_fea17c4dbee06037d5c354cfb4723e2a2a23262b8d88662aa4c84c54cd42d70d"],"source_ids":["src_f5aca28d20435bad9211aa6f4356a910"],"text":"The skill is triggered by natural-language phrases such as 'simmer this', 'refine this', 'hone this', or 'polish this'; any request to iteratively improve an artifact starts the loop.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_fd0693d501d68ee4c34de0a095b0e028adf606970f64c7503cca806342b66218","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"2389-research/simmer@73089c6f2224 snapshot 0c3030b83e9b2b41","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1323a5611062ffbdb9f864f5357c5746d5eaed62f5ae94bebb1633f8dd469c26","slc_ea0cf0ad7ad0d7706d8cfe0638daf9a1a515d4fdd247ce2fffa7725c26271cd9"],"source_ids":["src_f5aca28d20435bad9211aa6f4356a910"],"text":"The plugin ships one skill (simmer) with four subskills running the loop: Setup (identify artifact, elicit criteria), Generator (improve from ASI), Judge (score 1-10 per criterion, produce ASI), and Reflect (record trajectory, track best candidate).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_83af74e3807247a9950f9d662eeefa2e"}
